        "entity": 17592186068504,
        "text": "Calculate ∫1x2−2x+3dx.\nSolution:\nFirst, we complete the square in the denominator:\nx2−2x+3=x2−2⋅x+(12−12)+3=(x2−2⋅x+12)−1+3=(x−1)2+2\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n∫1x2−2x+3dx=∫1(x−1)2+2dx=12∫11+((x−1)/2)2dx.\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n∫11+u2du=arctan⁡u+C.\nThe only difference is that instead of u as the variable, we have (x−12).\nSo, let's perform the substitution\nu=x−12.\nDifferentiating, we get\ndudx=12⟹dx=2du.\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of u, and evaluate:\n∫1x2−2x+3dx=12∫11+((x−1)/2)2dx=12∫11+u2⋅2du=22∫11+u2du=22arctanu+C=22arctan(x−12)+C\n",
        "hasRawBold": false
      },
      {
        "entity": 17592186068506,
        "text": "Evaluate the integral ∫1+2/331|x−1|x2−2xdx.\nSolution:\nFirst, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\nx2−2x=x2−2x+(1−1)=(x2−2x+1)−1=(x−1)2−1\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n∫1+2/331|x−1|x2−2xdx=∫1+2/331|x−1|(x−1)2−1dx.\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n∫1|u|u2−1du=arcsecu+C\nThe only difference is that instead of u as the variable, we have x−1.\nSo, let's perform the substitution\nu=x−1.\nDifferentiating, we get\ndudx=1⟹dx=du.\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from x to u.\n\n\n\nx\n1+23\n3\n\n\n\nu\n23\n2\n\n\nTherefore,\n∫1+2/331|x−1|x2−2xdx=∫1+2/331|x−1|(x−1)2−1dx=∫2/321|u|u2−1du=arcsecu|2/32=arcsec(2)−arcsec(23)=(π3−π6)=π6.\n",
        "hasRawBold": false
      }
    ],
